1
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:05,890
This meat's so good!

2
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:07,930
It's so tender!

3
00:00:07,930 --> 00:00:10,860
Is the one you've got there Breakfast Set B?

4
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:13,370
Nope, Set C.

5
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:15,850
That one was good, too...

6
00:00:16,890 --> 00:00:19,530
A through E were all delicious!

7
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:24,390
What do you think, Chris? 
I'm going to start over with A again.

8
00:00:24,390 --> 00:00:27,390
Of course, so will I.

9
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:31,260
Crap! Crap! I overslept!

10
00:00:31,810 --> 00:00:35,450
You were supposed to wake me up, Rati!

11
00:00:35,450 --> 00:00:37,220
Why did you oversleep?

12
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:39,750
Thanks to you, I overslept too!

13
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:42,570
Have your roommate wake you up!

14
00:00:42,570 --> 00:00:46,540
I told them they didn't have to, 
because you were going to do it!

15
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:49,420
Well, that's your problem.

16
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:54,500
How much are you lot eating for breakfast?!

17
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:58,180
The three of you ate all this?

18
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:01,740
No, I just had this one plate.

19
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:03,540
So the <i>two</i> of you ate all this?

20
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:05,120
Isn't that too much food for breakfast?

21
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:07,430
It's normal, isn't it, Chris?

22
00:01:07,430 --> 00:01:10,380
Breakfast is the most 
important meal of the day.

23
00:01:12,210 --> 00:01:16,090
We need the energy to get us 
through the day ahead!

24
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:20,060
No, you've already eaten 
enough for three days.

25
00:01:21,510 --> 00:01:24,200
You were amazing yesterday!

26
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:26,720
You beat those three golems by yourself!

27
00:01:27,030 --> 00:01:28,280
Thanks.

28
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:31,390
Hey, don't push me!

29
00:01:31,390 --> 00:01:32,600
I'm not pushing you.

30
00:01:34,070 --> 00:01:36,340
I'm Rati, from the squire program.

31
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:38,180
This is Pram, from the knights.

32
00:01:38,180 --> 00:01:39,390
Hi, I'm Pram.

33
00:01:39,950 --> 00:01:41,860
Nice to meet you.

34
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:44,530
I'm Rafinha, from the knights.

35
00:01:44,530 --> 00:01:46,510
I'm Inglis, from the squires.

36
00:01:46,510 --> 00:01:47,790
Nice to meet you!

37
00:01:47,790 --> 00:01:49,830
Leone, from the knights. Hi.

38
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:54,170
Whisper, whisper, whisper, whisper.

39
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:54,170
I think people are staring.

40
00:01:54,170 --> 00:01:57,640
Oh, that's because of me...

41
00:01:57,640 --> 00:02:04,110
A-Ah. Well, I'm not from this country, 
so that stuff doesn't mean much to me.

42
00:02:04,110 --> 00:02:06,060
Where are you from?

43
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:08,590
Alucard. Same as Pram.

44
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:11,200
So you're exchange students.

45
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:14,610
Yeah. This place is nice and warm...

46
00:02:14,610 --> 00:02:17,390
Rati, we have to finish eating!
Class is gonna start!

47
00:02:17,390 --> 00:02:19,330
Oops, sorry!

48
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:21,420
Pram, let's hurry up and order!

49
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:23,280
We'll go with you.

50
00:02:23,610 --> 00:02:24,850
Let's get extra-large portions!

51
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:26,600
You're still eating?!

52
00:02:41,090 --> 00:02:44,050
<u>Reborn</u>

53
00:02:41,090 --> 00:02:44,050
to Master the Blade
     From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

54
00:02:41,090 --> 00:02:44,050
to Master the Blade
From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

55
00:03:57,090 --> 00:04:01,460
Episode 6     Labyrinth of Trials

56
00:03:57,370 --> 00:04:02,050
I'm Margoose, the practical 
instructor for you freshmen!

57
00:04:02,050 --> 00:04:06,880
Today we'll be doing a Flying Gear 
exercise with both the knights and squires.

58
00:04:07,110 --> 00:04:08,980
I want to start by making one thing clear:

59
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:13,300
Our war isn't just against 
the magicite beasts!

60
00:04:13,580 --> 00:04:14,790
We war against ourselves,

61
00:04:14,790 --> 00:04:18,260
pushing ourselves to the limit 
to bring peace and safety to the people!

62
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:21,720
And that starts with training our bodies!

63
00:04:22,050 --> 00:04:25,820
So we're all going to run 
to the Flying Gear dock!

64
00:04:26,960 --> 00:04:30,700
And the Flying Gears are already 
out of the equation.

65
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:33,710
Get moving! Double time!

66
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:35,670
He's fast! I'm already losing sight of him!

67
00:04:36,350 --> 00:04:38,630
Where's the Flying Gear dock?

68
00:04:38,630 --> 00:04:42,020
I saw it yesterday. It's pretty far.

69
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:44,140
We need to keep up with him!

70
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:46,080
This is a nice change of pace.

71
00:04:46,790 --> 00:04:49,850
But just running there normally 
wouldn't be any fun at all.

72
00:04:49,850 --> 00:04:53,320
<i>I'll try that gravity effect that 
Principal Miliera used yesterday.</i>

73
00:04:54,190 --> 00:04:56,260
<i>First, I convert my aether to mana...</i>

74
00:04:56,790 --> 00:04:59,220
<i>And then, the way she set up her mana was...</i>

75
00:05:01,270 --> 00:05:04,030
<i>Okay, that'll do for now.</i>

76
00:05:05,220 --> 00:05:08,200
<i>If I get better, 
I bet I can make it heavier!</i>

77
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:10,990
Seriously? How is she so fast?

78
00:05:11,460 --> 00:05:15,080
Inglis was still standing there 
when we left...

79
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:17,790
Don't worry. Chris is...

80
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:20,500
See?

81
00:05:22,630 --> 00:05:24,800
Leone, lets pick up the pace.

82
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:25,910
Huh? Okay!

83
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:35,800
Rati, wait! Jeez!

84
00:05:37,340 --> 00:05:39,270
Don't hurt yourselves trying to keep up!

85
00:05:39,270 --> 00:05:44,260
You're not expected to match 
my speed from the start...

86
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:47,950
Can I go on ahead?

87
00:05:47,950 --> 00:05:49,330
S-Sure.

88
00:05:49,330 --> 00:05:50,520
What's your name?

89
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:52,090
Inglis Eucus.

90
00:05:52,090 --> 00:05:54,320
You've got potential!

91
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:55,750
Very good!

92
00:05:55,750 --> 00:05:58,790
Wait up!

93
00:05:58,790 --> 00:06:00,340
Wow! Not bad!

94
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:05,830
Damn it! You're not even breaking 
a sweat, and I'm dying here!

95
00:06:07,190 --> 00:06:10,560
Looks like this year's 
freshmen have potential!

96
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:11,880
Good, good.

97
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:13,420
Don't forget me.

98
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:18,500
W-We managed to catch up...

99
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:22,370
I don't think Chris is using 
her full strength yet.

100
00:06:24,470 --> 00:06:28,820
I'm not gonna lose, even if it kills me!

101
00:06:29,390 --> 00:06:31,290
<i>That's the spirit!</i>

102
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:33,010
I'll be going on ahead!

103
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:35,350
How is she doing that?

104
00:06:35,750 --> 00:06:38,710
I told you. She wasn't 
using her full strength.

105
00:06:39,210 --> 00:06:44,170
If I tried to catch up to her, 
I might actually die.

106
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:51,890
Wow!

107
00:06:51,890 --> 00:06:55,740
It's kind of exciting to look at, 
isn't it, Chris?

108
00:06:55,740 --> 00:06:57,050
It sure is, Rani.

109
00:06:57,740 --> 00:07:01,530
This is the Royal Academy. 
It's got the latest technology.

110
00:07:03,730 --> 00:07:07,890
Now, form up into groups. 
Two or three to a Flying Gear.

111
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:10,240
Once it's outside, get on board!

112
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:11,870
One of you takes the controls.

113
00:07:12,170 --> 00:07:15,320
The others, hang on tight 
and make sure you don't fall off!

114
00:07:15,870 --> 00:07:17,820
Can I go first?

115
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:19,180
Sure!

116
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:22,910
Squires spend a lot of time 
piloting Flying Gears, after all.

117
00:07:23,230 --> 00:07:25,380
Good luck, Inglis!

118
00:07:31,060 --> 00:07:34,260
The instructions for flying it 
are on the panel in front of you.

119
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:38,010
After you activate the engine, 
switch it to flight mode.

120
00:07:39,890 --> 00:07:44,610
When the wings on both sides deploy, 
slowly bring up the accelerator.

121
00:07:49,520 --> 00:07:52,730
Wow, we're flying!

122
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:55,050
Keep it up, Chris!

123
00:07:55,050 --> 00:07:56,210
Yeah...

124
00:07:56,210 --> 00:07:57,410
This is gonna work!

125
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:01,960
This feels so good!

126
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:03,880
And the scenery's beautiful!

127
00:08:05,090 --> 00:08:07,480
Aren't we going a little too fast?

128
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:09,280
I'm kind of scared...

129
00:08:09,630 --> 00:08:12,630
But we're going to use these 
to fight the magicite beasts, right?

130
00:08:12,630 --> 00:08:13,920
Better get used to it.

131
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:15,070
That's right!

132
00:08:15,070 --> 00:08:16,940
And this is the best way!

133
00:08:19,250 --> 00:08:21,010
Wow, Rati!

134
00:08:21,010 --> 00:08:22,230
You're really good at this!

135
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:28,640
Looks like when it comes 
to Flying Gears, I win!

136
00:08:29,070 --> 00:08:30,680
I'll catch up to him.

137
00:08:35,610 --> 00:08:37,410
What are you doing?

138
00:08:37,810 --> 00:08:40,370
I hate to lose.

139
00:08:40,370 --> 00:08:43,130
L-Looks like... freshmen... potential!

140
00:08:43,130 --> 00:08:44,660
Good...

141
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:49,830
Wow, she's amazing.

142
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:53,040
Not only is she pretty, 
the things she does are incredible.

143
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:57,670
Why are you talking like that 
when you've already got me, Rati?

144
00:08:57,670 --> 00:08:58,350
Like what?

145
00:08:58,350 --> 00:09:05,260
You never call me pretty! It's not fair!

146
00:09:01,970 --> 00:09:05,260
Stop it! That's dangerous!

147
00:09:24,930 --> 00:09:28,210
I'm sure you're tired after your classes,

148
00:09:28,210 --> 00:09:32,680
but we've got a special test for you today.

149
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:36,160
If I call your name, step forward.

150
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:35,770
A special test....

151
00:09:36,390 --> 00:09:41,100
Rafinha. Liselotte. Leone. Pram.

152
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:42,090
Yes, ma'am!

153
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:46,560
Y-Yes, ma'am!

154
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:50,580
You four are the students that have been 
recommended from the knight program.

155
00:09:50,580 --> 00:09:52,520
And also Inglis...

156
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:53,500
Yes, ma'am.

157
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:58,190
You've been recommended 
from the squire program.

158
00:09:58,870 --> 00:10:02,200
Hey, is that the test that 
everyone was talking about?

159
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:05,980
Yes! It's a huge honor just 
to be recommended for it,

160
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:09,290
since it means the academy 
thinks you've got potential!

161
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:13,300
The test is simple.

162
00:10:13,300 --> 00:10:17,100
I'm going to send you somewhere.

163
00:10:17,740 --> 00:10:21,180
Come back here before the time limit is up.

164
00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:24,300
If you can do that, you pass!

165
00:10:24,670 --> 00:10:26,470
Where is "somewhere"?

166
00:10:26,470 --> 00:10:29,280
A special space created by an Artifact!

167
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:34,030
We call it the Labyrinth of Trials.

168
00:10:34,030 --> 00:10:39,480
It will test not only your strength, 
but your mental fortitude as well.

169
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:41,200
Mental fortitude...

170
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:45,200
You might find yourself suffering...

171
00:10:45,610 --> 00:10:50,030
But the goal is to enhance 
your mental strength as knights.

172
00:10:50,030 --> 00:10:51,190
Understood?

173
00:10:51,190 --> 00:10:51,910
Yes, ma'am!

174
00:10:53,310 --> 00:10:54,540
You okay?

175
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:59,100
I won't let you beat me!

176
00:11:00,140 --> 00:11:04,180
<i>She appears to view me as a rival 
for some reason, but...</i>

177
00:11:06,170 --> 00:11:07,560
<i>No matter.</i>

178
00:11:12,090 --> 00:11:14,470
Pick a door.

179
00:11:14,790 --> 00:11:19,790
Each of you will find an 
appropriate trial beyond it.

180
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:22,360
Now, let the test begin!

181
00:11:23,450 --> 00:11:25,930
Rani, Leone, be careful!

182
00:11:25,930 --> 00:11:27,010
You too, Chris!

183
00:11:27,010 --> 00:11:28,120
Let's do our best!

184
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:30,370
I know I can do this!

185
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:12,150
<i>This is... every foe I've ever fought!</i>

186
00:12:12,670 --> 00:12:14,910
<i>The perfect test!</i>

187
00:12:14,910 --> 00:12:16,000
Here I go!

188
00:12:16,930 --> 00:12:18,060
What?

189
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:23,640
This isn't a test...

190
00:12:25,380 --> 00:12:26,720
Chris...

191
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:27,700
Rani?

192
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:40,330
Memories from my youth?

193
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:44,670
<i>I just keep going back 
through my memories...</i>

194
00:12:44,670 --> 00:12:46,510
<i>No enemies to be seen.</i>

195
00:12:59,010 --> 00:13:01,600
<i>I've returned to when I was newly born.</i>

196
00:13:02,790 --> 00:13:06,510
<i>Is this the end? No...</i>

197
00:13:07,510 --> 00:13:08,980
These are...

198
00:13:12,170 --> 00:13:15,160
memories of my last life?

199
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:21,060
Your Highness...

200
00:13:22,750 --> 00:13:24,060
<i>That voice...</i>

201
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:31,480
It's been many years, Your Highness.

202
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:33,600
Randall...

203
00:13:34,220 --> 00:13:37,910
<i>My heir, and the man who was set 
to inherit the kingdom after my death.</i>

204
00:13:37,910 --> 00:13:42,050
If you're really Randall, 
I'd like to know why, after I died,

205
00:13:42,050 --> 00:13:46,600
some people in this world started thinking 
of themselves as better than others.

206
00:13:47,850 --> 00:13:51,300
But you won't have an answer 
for me, will you?

207
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:53,470
That is correct, Your Majesty!

208
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:59,420
<i>This isn't good.</i>

209
00:14:02,530 --> 00:14:06,870
<i>If I keep going, I might end up 
running into the Goddess Alistia.</i>

210
00:14:07,230 --> 00:14:12,320
This was supposed to be a test of 
mental strength? I don't like it.

211
00:14:16,450 --> 00:14:20,210
I've got better things to do 
than waste my time here.

212
00:14:29,650 --> 00:14:31,340
There's more up there?

213
00:14:31,340 --> 00:14:33,140
Wh-What was that?

214
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:36,230
I see!

215
00:14:36,230 --> 00:14:38,560
So it's connected to the spaces 
where the others are?

216
00:14:39,070 --> 00:14:41,850
Did you do this?

217
00:14:41,850 --> 00:14:45,520
Yeah. I didn't feel like 
continuing straight ahead.

218
00:14:45,910 --> 00:14:49,620
How could she destroy such a strange space?

219
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:52,710
Just who are you?

220
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:59,560
Just a simple squire,

221
00:15:00,280 --> 00:15:02,180
in Rafinha Bilford's service.

222
00:15:03,220 --> 00:15:09,280
If you're her squire, tell her not 
to hate her classmate so much.

223
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:13,890
I'm not here to be her enemy.

224
00:15:14,650 --> 00:15:17,730
I don't think she hates you.

225
00:15:17,730 --> 00:15:18,830
She does!

226
00:15:18,830 --> 00:15:23,900
She tries to stay away from me as best 
she can and won't look me in the eye!

227
00:15:24,630 --> 00:15:29,360
Then maybe she's upset 
with the way you treat Leone.

228
00:15:29,810 --> 00:15:33,710
I'm the daughter of this 
kingdom's chancellor.

229
00:15:33,710 --> 00:15:36,170
I need to be careful.

230
00:15:37,130 --> 00:15:39,380
Though, to be honest...

231
00:15:39,380 --> 00:15:40,620
Oh?

232
00:15:42,470 --> 00:15:46,460
I do feel I went a little too far.

233
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:49,580
Okay. I'll tell her for you.

234
00:15:50,050 --> 00:15:52,260
So, you think we can get out of here?

235
00:15:53,140 --> 00:15:56,740
I'm sick of this place. It just 
brings back all my bad memories.

236
00:15:56,740 --> 00:15:58,400
Me too.

237
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:01,750
So I figured I'd bust my way out.

238
00:16:01,750 --> 00:16:02,730
Want to join me?

239
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:05,140
That sounds fun.

240
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:06,880
Let's go together.

241
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:08,600
Okay, let's go.

242
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:09,680
Wait.

243
00:16:18,110 --> 00:16:21,570
Is that your Gift?

244
00:16:21,570 --> 00:16:24,540
Yes. I'll take you to the top.

245
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:28,350
Wow!

246
00:16:28,350 --> 00:16:29,720
You don't even need a Flying Gear!

247
00:16:29,970 --> 00:16:32,480
Stop! What are you doing to my brother?

248
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:35,560
Move! You're wrong about this!

249
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:39,570
That's... Leon?

250
00:16:40,270 --> 00:16:43,320
My brother's a holy knight now!

251
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:45,590
He's an inspiration to everyone!

252
00:16:45,590 --> 00:16:47,550
Why are you being so mean?

253
00:16:48,010 --> 00:16:49,920
It's all a lie!

254
00:16:49,920 --> 00:16:51,520
You'll understand some day!

255
00:16:52,170 --> 00:16:56,630
Curse you! And on the very day 
my son became a holy knight!

256
00:16:56,630 --> 00:16:58,490
What are you going to do to Leon?

257
00:16:58,490 --> 00:17:01,460
Mother... Father...

258
00:17:01,830 --> 00:17:05,460
<i>Those wounds... She's already 
expended a great deal of her mana.</i>

259
00:17:06,330 --> 00:17:10,160
<i>She must have overcome many 
fierce battles to reach this point.</i>

260
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:15,580
I'll... I'll defeat you 
and keep going forward!

261
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:18,380
I'll defeat my brother Leon!

262
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:22,570
Go on ahead. I'll help her.

263
00:17:24,010 --> 00:17:28,090
I won't let you take another step forward, 
if you're going to hurt my child!

264
00:17:28,090 --> 00:17:30,510
Begone! Go!

265
00:17:30,930 --> 00:17:33,730
I'll protect Leon, 
even at the cost of my life!

266
00:17:38,070 --> 00:17:40,570
Begone, traitor!

267
00:17:41,650 --> 00:17:43,330
Sorry to interrupt!

268
00:17:46,260 --> 00:17:48,070
I-Inglis?

269
00:17:48,070 --> 00:17:49,660
I'm glad I made it.

270
00:17:51,870 --> 00:17:53,500
How did you get here?

271
00:17:54,490 --> 00:17:55,960
I broke through the walls.

272
00:17:56,320 --> 00:17:58,140
That's crazy...

273
00:17:58,140 --> 00:18:00,580
That's not how the test is supposed to work.

274
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:02,440
Nobody said I couldn't!

275
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:05,250
I won't let you hurt my brother!

276
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:07,400
I'll protect Leon, no matter what!

277
00:18:09,870 --> 00:18:11,310
Inglis?

278
00:18:11,310 --> 00:18:12,620
I'll handle them.

279
00:18:18,990 --> 00:18:20,740
Y-You're...

280
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:24,020
It's hard for you or your friends 
to fight them, right?

281
00:18:24,020 --> 00:18:26,590
It's easier for me.

282
00:18:26,590 --> 00:18:28,700
Yeah, thanks.

283
00:18:30,260 --> 00:18:32,510
Th-Thank you.

284
00:18:32,510 --> 00:18:36,880
I'd like to apologize for 
hurting you the other day.

285
00:18:37,550 --> 00:18:38,660
I'm sorry.

286
00:18:39,310 --> 00:18:40,900
No, it's not...

287
00:18:41,130 --> 00:18:44,020
Liselotte's actually a nice girl, huh?

288
00:18:44,020 --> 00:18:46,840
That "actually" was unnecessary!

289
00:18:50,020 --> 00:18:53,420
Now, let's head for the top floor.

290
00:18:55,870 --> 00:18:57,730
Hurry up!

291
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:04,530
Wow!

292
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:07,700
She doesn't even need a Flying Gear, right?

293
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:09,830
You just said that!

294
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:12,780
Welcome back.

295
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:15,480
I guess we made it out.

296
00:19:15,940 --> 00:19:16,750
Yeah.

297
00:19:17,140 --> 00:19:18,670
Huh?

298
00:19:18,670 --> 00:19:22,390
You came out of a different door 
than the one you went in!

299
00:19:22,390 --> 00:19:25,370
And the three of you all 
came out of the same door?

300
00:19:25,370 --> 00:19:28,760
Nothing really unusual happened.

301
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:30,720
Really?

302
00:19:31,590 --> 00:19:33,620
That's a huge lie.

303
00:19:33,270 --> 00:19:36,270
Maybe it's broken...

304
00:19:33,620 --> 00:19:36,280
You two helped me on the way, too...

305
00:19:36,810 --> 00:19:39,090
You don't want to do it 
all over again, right?

306
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:44,400
Principal Miliera, 
this means we passed, right?

307
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:48,050
Well, you did come out of the door.

308
00:19:48,050 --> 00:19:50,660
So I guess I have to pass you.

309
00:19:51,220 --> 00:19:54,140
You pass. Congratulations!

310
00:19:56,160 --> 00:19:57,600
Where are Rani and Pram?

311
00:19:58,060 --> 00:19:59,920
Oh, did she pass already?

312
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:03,240
No, she failed almost immediately.

313
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:05,810
A hole opened, and she got tossed out.

314
00:20:06,270 --> 00:20:09,520
I was supposed to win this!

315
00:20:09,780 --> 00:20:12,360
I told you to give it up.

316
00:20:13,270 --> 00:20:14,360
Rani!

317
00:20:14,360 --> 00:20:15,360
Chris!

318
00:20:15,790 --> 00:20:17,950
I finally made it out!

319
00:20:18,860 --> 00:20:21,400
Rafinha, you pass!

320
00:20:21,710 --> 00:20:23,570
Welcome back, Rani!

321
00:20:23,570 --> 00:20:24,680
Congratulations!

322
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:25,900
Thank you!

323
00:20:25,900 --> 00:20:28,150
You two both passed, right?

324
00:20:28,150 --> 00:20:29,930
Huh? Oh, of course.

325
00:20:29,930 --> 00:20:31,400
I guess...

326
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:33,080
You guess?

327
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:34,210
Never mind.

328
00:20:34,210 --> 00:20:35,900
Anyway, were you okay?

329
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:38,040
I'm so tired!

330
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:40,890
I'm gonna eat a lot and then sleep!

331
00:20:41,350 --> 00:20:44,350
When you're tired, you move 
around in your sleep a lot.

332
00:20:44,350 --> 00:20:46,430
It's going to be a rough night.

333
00:20:46,430 --> 00:20:48,690
That's so mean, Chris!

334
00:20:48,690 --> 00:20:51,170
S-Sorry, it's my fault...

335
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:54,930
No! No! That's not what I meant!

336
00:20:54,930 --> 00:20:56,430
If that's what this is about...

337
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:02,690
You gonna be okay, Leone?

338
00:21:02,690 --> 00:21:04,780
I-I'm fine.

339
00:21:04,780 --> 00:21:06,190
It'll be fine.

340
00:21:06,190 --> 00:21:08,750
Liselotte's actually a good girl.

341
00:21:08,750 --> 00:21:10,240
Yeah, I know.

342
00:21:11,870 --> 00:21:15,460
Why are you standing outside 
my room and talking about me?

343
00:21:17,550 --> 00:21:19,930
Welcome to <i>our</i> room!

344
00:21:19,930 --> 00:21:22,660
Th-Thanks for having me.

345
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:25,250
Now, come inside.

346
00:21:29,180 --> 00:21:30,600
Hey...

347
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:34,550
I was just kidding.

348
00:21:34,780 --> 00:21:37,760
Liselotte can be surprisingly silly.

349
00:21:38,030 --> 00:21:41,240
I'd prefer you said I had a sense of humor.

350
00:21:41,530 --> 00:21:44,040
Wow, this room is so cute!

351
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:46,870
This isn't the furniture 
that came with the room!

352
00:21:46,870 --> 00:21:49,440
I brought in the same kind I have at home!

353
00:21:49,810 --> 00:21:54,020
Hey, I brought a lot of party things 
so we could have a celebration!

354
00:21:54,020 --> 00:21:55,670
A celebration of what?

355
00:21:55,670 --> 00:22:00,520
You know... making up... and stuff.

356
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:03,100
I brought lots of food, too!

357
00:22:03,100 --> 00:22:06,830
You've still got room for food 
after all you ate at dinner?!

358
